hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16196","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid, meaning Abu Maslamah, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd narrated to us, he said: I heard a man say to Ibn al-Zubayr: Give us fatwa on jar nabidh. So he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it."
"16197","Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) open prayer and raise his hands until he passed with them his ears."
"16198","It was read to Sufyan, and I was present: I heard Ibn Ajlan and Ziyad ibn Sad, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate thus, and Ibn al-Zubayr clenched."
"16199","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he sat in tashahhud put his right hand on his right thigh and his left hand on his left thigh, and pointed with the forefinger, and his sight did not go beyond his pointing."
"16200","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abidah, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a man swore by Allah, who there is no god but He, falsely, and Allah forgave him. Shubah said: Because of tawhid."
"16201","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from Mansur from Mujahid from Yusuf from Ibn al-Zubayr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: You are the eldest child of your father, so perform Hajj on his behalf."
"16202","He said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me from Ibn Ishaq, he said: My father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, he said: While we were in Makkah, Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr came out to us and forbade tamattu of Umrah with Hajj and denied that the people had done that with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). That reached Abdullah ibn Abbas and he said: What does Ibn al-Zubayr know about this? Let him return to his mother Asma bint Abi Bakr and ask her, for if al-Zubayr had not returned to her in a state of permissibility and she had become permissible. That reached Asma and she said: May Allah forgive Ibn Abbas; by Allah, he spoke harshly. By Allah, Ibn Abbas has spoken the truth; they exited ihram and we exited ihram and they were with women."
"16203","He said: Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Thabit narrated to me that between Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr and his brother Amr ibn al-Zubayr there was a dispute, so Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr entered upon Said ibn al-As while Amr ibn al-Zubayr was with him on the couch. Said said to Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr: Here. He said: No; the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), is that the two litigants sit before the judge."
"16204","Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Urwah, narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr used to say at the end of every prayer when he gave the salam: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise and He is over all things capable; there is no change nor power except with Allah; there is no god but Allah and we worship none but Him; to Him belong blessing and bounty and fine praise; there is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion even if the disbelievers dislike it. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to declare Allah's oneness with them at the end of every prayer."
"16205","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Nafi, meaning Ibn Umar, narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, then Ibn al-Zubayr said: After this verse Umar would not hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without asking him to make him understand, meaning His saying, Exalted is He: Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet."
"16206","Mamar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Al-Hajjaj narrated to us from Furat ibn Abdullah, and he is Furat al-Qazzaz, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, and Ibn al-Zubayr had put him over the judiciary, when the letter of Ibn al-Zubayr came to him: Peace be upon you; as for what follows, you wrote asking me about the grandfather, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take a close friend from this ummah besides my Lord, Mighty and Majestic is He, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah, but he is my brother in religion and my companion in the cave. He made the grandfather a father, and the truest thing we have taken is the saying of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him."
"16207","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Wahb ibn Kaysan, the freedman of Ibn al-Zubayr, narrated to me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr on the day of Eid saying, when he had prayed before the sermon then stood addressing the people: O people, such is the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16208","He said: Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, he said: Nafi ibn Thabit informed me from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Isha, he bowed four rakahs and made witr with one prostration, then slept until he prayed after his prayer at night."
"16209","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Hisham, he said: My father informed me from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suck and two sucks from nursing do not prohibit."
"16210","Arim narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Musab ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us from his father, he said: Qutaylah bint Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Asad of Banu Malik ibn Hisl came to her daughter Asma bint Abi Bakr with gifts of lizards and aqt and ghee, and she was a polytheist, so Asma refused to accept her gift and to admit her into her house. Aishah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, sent down: Allah does not forbid you regarding those who did not fight you in religion, to the end of the verse. So he ordered her to accept her gift and to admit her into her house."
"16211","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take a close friend besides Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, until I meet Him, I would have taken Abu Bakr, he made the grandfather a father."
"16212","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr, the son of my paternal aunt."
"16213","Yahya and Waki narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah in mursal form."
"16214","Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us in mursal form; Ibn al-Zubayr is not in it."
"16215","He said: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: And Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: A man of the Ansar disputed with al-Zubayr before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the channels of al-Harrah with which they watered the date palms. The Ansari said to al-Zubayr: Let the water flow, but he refused, so he spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Irrigate, O Zubayr, then send on to your neighbor. The Ansari became angry and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is the son of your aunt? So his face changed color, then he said: Withhold the water until it reaches the walls. Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, I think this verse was sent down concerning that: But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what has arisen between them, to His saying: and submit fully."
"16216","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: Habib al-Muallim narrated to us from Ata from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in other mosques except the Sacred Mosque, and a prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred prayers in this one."
"16217","He said: Yunus and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; Affan said in his hadith: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, and Yunus said: from Thabit, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr; Affan said: addressing us, and Yunus said: while he was addressing, saying: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"16218","He said: Al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, he said: Thuwayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying: This is the day of Ashura, so fast, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast it."
"16219","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abi Mulaykah from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The one to whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were to take a close friend besides Allah until I meet Him, I would have taken Abu Bakr, he made the grandfather a father."
"16220","He said: Waki narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us from his father from Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suck and two sucks do not prohibit."
"16221","He said: Ismail narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr addressing upon this minbar, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the salam at the end of the prayer, or the prayers, he would say: There is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise and He is over all things capable; there is no change nor power except with Allah, and we worship none but Him, people of blessing and bounty and fine praise; there is no god but Allah, sincere to Him in religion even if the disbelievers dislike it."
"16222","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub informed us from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr that Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Fatimah is only a part of me; what harms her harms me and what wearies her wearies me."
"16223","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr about the earthen jar and the gourd."
"16224","Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Mujahid from Yusuf ibn al-Zubayr from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: A man of Khatham came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My father was reached by Islam while he is a very old man unable to ride the camel, and Hajj is prescribed for him; shall I perform Hajj for him? He said: Are you his eldest child? He said: Yes. He said: Tell me, if your father had a debt and you paid it for him, would that suffice for him? He said: Yes. He said: Then perform Hajj for him."
"16225","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us from Ayyub from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Qarn as the miqat for the people of Najd."
"16226","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us from Mansur from Mujahid from Ibn al-Zubayr that Zamah had a slave girl whom he used to have intercourse with, and they suspected her, then she gave birth, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sawdah: As for inheritance, it is his, but as for you, veil yourself from him, O Sawdah, for he is not your brother."
"16227","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Uyaynah informed us from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid from al-Shabi, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr while he was leaning upon the Kabah, saying: By the Lord of this Kabah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed so-and-so and what was born of his loins."
"16228","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Hisham ibn Urwah from his father, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said to Abdullah ibn Jafar: Do you remember the day we went out to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he carried me and left you? And he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be met by boys when he came from a journey."
"16229","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us; Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashi narrated to me from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Announce marriage."
"16230","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from Abu Maslamah that he heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Usayd, he said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr, and a man asked him about nabidh of the earthen jar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade nabidh of the earthen jar."
"16231","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Israil narrated to us from Thuwayr, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr while upon the minbar saying: This is the day of Ashura, so fast, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered its fast."
"16232","Waki narrated to us: Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: The two good ones, Abu Bakr and Umar, almost perished when the delegation of Banu Tamim came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them pointed to al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Hanzali, the brother of Banu Mujashi, and the other pointed to someone else. Abu Bakr said to Umar: You only meant to oppose me, so Umar said: I did not mean to oppose you. Then their voices rose in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so there was sent down: O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet, to His saying: great. Ibn Abi Mulaykah said: Ibn al-Zubayr said: After that, when Umar spoke to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention that about his father, meaning Abu Bakr, he spoke to him like one confiding a secret; he could not hear him until he asked him to make him understand."
